# Pulumi Infrastructure Conventions

## File Layout

All resources in `infra/resources/`:
- `functions.py` — Cloud Function definitions
- `workflow.py` — Cloud Workflow
- `scheduler.py` — Cloud Scheduler jobs
- `firestore.py` — Firestore indexes and rules
- `api_gateway.py` — API Gateway for frontend
- `secrets.py` — Secret Manager resources
- `iam.py` — IAM bindings (explicit, never default service accounts)

## Resource Naming

```python
import pulumi
env = pulumi.get_stack()  # "staging" or "prod"
name = f"kalilos-{env}-create-report"
```

## Adding a New Cloud Function

Follow the pattern in `infra/resources/functions.py`:

```python
create_report_fn = gcp.cloudfunctionsv2.Function(
    f"kalilos-{env}-create-report",
    location=region,
    build_config={"runtime": "python312", "entry_point": "handler", "source": {...}},
    service_config={"available_memory": "256M", "environment_variables": {...}},
)
```

## Stack Configuration

- `Pulumi.staging.yaml` → GCP project `kalilos-connector-staging`
- `Pulumi.prod.yaml` → GCP project `kalilos-connector-prod`

## Rules

- Always define IAM bindings explicitly in `iam.py`
- Never use default service accounts — create dedicated ones per function group
- Deploy via `make deploy-infra`, never raw `pulumi up`
